Z||000000||Bluebottlejunky||03-11-2001||12:10 PM||||Ok,  I have been thinking alot about what I want to do with my fiero right now.  I have an 85 GT pretty much mint on inside of car, no rips, little bit of fading, its loaded with pm, pl, pw, power turnk release.  My plan from the start was to do the inside black and red, with mr mikes leather.  But I keep hearing "why would you want to do all that stuff to a pretty much stock great looking interior.  What do you guys think?<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85' GT 4sp||||reg||5
Z||000001||Formula88||03-11-2001||12:13 PM||||It it's what you want, do it!  If the interior is in great shape, save it so you can re-install it later, or sell it to someone who needs it.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000002||JBGehling||03-11-2001||03:10 PM||||I'm in the same situation... I have an 88 GT with PERFECT interior and I'm thinking about redoing the seats w/ Mr. Mike's leather. <BR>Here's my plan:<BR>Get the seat covers and get some old seats from the junkyard to put them on, then take the stock seats out and keep them in my room  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">.||||reg||1
Z||000003||TwisT||03-11-2001||04:03 PM||||Boy this sounds familiar.  <P>I wanted to do the SAME thing (red and black) but already have a GREAT looking,  GREAT shape tan interior.<P>What I've elected to do is enhance what I've already got with some miscelanious peices...  white-faced gauges,  Momo steering wheel,  gate-style shifter,  carbon-fiber overlay here and there,  along with some chrome.  <P>It all depends on how you feel about your car,  and how much money you have into it.  I personally would go for it...  it's nice now,  and will be even "nicer" when you make it how you want it,  right?  =)<P>Good luck,  and if you decide to follow through with it,  be sure to keep us posted with pictures.  I LOVE the red and black!<P>Brett  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||tgowens||03-11-2001||05:15 PM||||TwisT, if you do anything to your interior you might want to save the original pieces as they are and find some gray pieces to paint/overlay, etc........the tan interior is much harder to find pieces for than the gray. And, the trim bezels are a color called Roman Bronze NOT Silver - the Silver parts are all over the place but you will have a hard time trying to replace the Bronze ones, especially the bezel around the shifter with the ash tray doors on it.||||reg||1
